<article class="env-remark" id="B68C62">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/B68C62">Remark <span data-tag="B68C62">6.1.4.4</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be a presentable $\infty $-category. Then for every simplicial resolution $U_{\bullet }^{+}$ in $\calX $, there is a map $f: U_{\bullet }^{+} \rightarrow V_{\bullet }^{+}$ which exhibits $V_{\bullet }^{+}$ as the groupoid resolution generated by $U_{\bullet }^{+}$. In view of the equivalence $\Res (\calX ) \rightarrow \calX _{\Delta }$, this is equivalent to the assertion that $\Grp (\calX )$ is a localization of $\calX _{\Delta }$. This follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/9B195B" data-tag="9B195B">6.1.2.6</a> together with Lemmas <a href="/tag/7C6D26" data-tag="7C6D26">5.5.4.18</a> and <a href="/tag/48CDAD" data-tag="48CDAD">5.5.4.19</a>. </p>
</article>